{"graph_chars": "A price floor is a legal minimum. The best-known is the minimum wage. Federal minimum in two thousand twenty-two was seven dollars twenty-five an hour, about fifteen thousand eighty a year if you work full time, a bit above the federal poverty line for a single person. Agricultural price supports are floors too. The European Union spends tens of billions of euros a year to keep farm prices up. Without intervention, wheat would clear at P-zero. A floor at P-F, above equilibrium, means quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded: a surplus. If the government buys the extra, farmers gain, taxpayers and food buyers pay. High-income countries spend roughly one billion dollars a day supporting farmers. A floor set below equilibrium does nothing. Same logic as a ceiling set above equilibrium: it is not binding.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0635], [0.0635, 0.1271], [0.1271, 0.1906], [0.1906, 0.2542], [0.2542, 0.3177], [0.3177, 0.3813], [0.3813, 0.4448], [0.4448, 0.5084], [0.5084, 0.5719], [0.5719, 0.6355], [0.6355, 0.699], [0.699, 0.7626], [0.7626, 0.8261], [0.8261, 0.8896], [0.8896, 0.9532], [0.9532, 1.0167], [1.0167, 1.0803], [1.0803, 1.1438], [1.1438, 1.2074], [1.2074, 1.2709], [1.2709, 1.3345], [1.3345, 1.398], [1.398, 1.4616], [1.4616, 1.5251], [1.5251, 1.5887], [1.5887, 1.6522], [1.6522, 1.7157], [1.7157, 1.7793], [1.7793, 1.8428], [1.8428, 1.9064], [1.9064, 1.9699], [1.9699, 2.0335], [2.0335, 2.097], [2.097, 2.1606], [2.1606, 2.2241], [2.2241, 2.2877], [2.2877, 2.3512], [2.3512, 2.4147], [2.4147, 2.4783], [2.4783, 2.5418], [2.5418, 2.6054], [2.6054, 2.6689], [2.6689, 2.7325], [2.7325, 2.796], [2.796, 2.8596], [2.8596, 2.9231], [2.9231, 2.9867], [2.9867, 3.0502], [3.0502, 3.1138], [3.1138, 3.1773], [3.1773, 3.2408], [3.2408, 3.3044], [3.3044, 3.3679], [3.3679, 3.4315], [3.4315, 3.495], [3.495, 3.5586], [3.5586, 3.6221], [3.6221, 3.6857], [3.6857, 3.7492], [3.7492, 3.8128], [3.8128, 3.8763], [3.8763, 3.9399], [3.9399, 4.0034], [4.0034, 4.0669], [4.0669, 4